    response = requests.get(
        f"https://api.example.com/users/{user_id}",
        timeout=10,
    )
    response.raise_for_status()
    return response.json()


def fetch_user(user_id: int) -> dict:
    return deepcopy(_fetch_user_cached(user_id))
```

The cache is local to each process and has no time-based expiration. Call `_fetch_user_cached.cache_clear()` to invalidate it when user data changes. Exceptions aren’t cached.

