In SwiftUI, call it with `.task { await model.load() }` so SwiftUI can cancel the load when the view disappears. The `isLoading` guard ignores overlapping calls while the first is suspended, and a failed refresh leaves the existing items intact. If `Parser.parse` can fail, make it `throws` and use `try` so parse failures reach `loadError` too.

`URLSession` suspends without blocking the main actor; **the synchronous parser still runs on it**. Keep that default unless profiling shows parsing causes UI stalls. If it does, move parsing into an `@concurrent` async helper, make the parser callable outside the main actor, and return `Sendable` items. Check cancellation again after awaiting the helper and before publishing its result.

